0 @I6000000006714876531@ INDI
1 NAME Viljo Gabriel /Rewell/
2 GIVN Viljo Gabriel
2 SURN Rewell
2 _MARNM Revell
1 NAME Viljo Revell
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 JAN 1910
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vaasa
3 CTRY Finland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 NOV 1964
2 ADDR
3 CITY Helsinki
3 CTRY Finland
1 OCCU Arkkitehti, architect
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Löjtnant på pansarskeppet Ilmarinen. En av 132 överlevande efter undergången 13.9 1941. 271 marinsoldater omkom. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viljo_Revell '''Viljo Gabriel Revell'''] was a Finnish architect of 
2 CONC the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functionalism_(architecture functionalist] school. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Internationally, Revell is''' best known for designing the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toronto_City_Hall New City Hall] of Toronto, Ontario, Canada, although it is nothing but functional, caused an enormous amount of conflic
2 CONC t at the times, but in hindsight it actually is of a world class design. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''At odds with''' that, in Finland he is best / worst known for the design (or lack thereof) of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lasipalatsi Lasipalatsi] ("Glass Palace", not very glassy), the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pal
2 CONC ace_Hotel,_Helsinki Palace Hotel], and the so-called [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City-Center Sausage Building], all in Helsinki. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The last one''' of these, the Sausage Building, located at the very heart of Helsinki, next to the Helsinki main railway station, greeting visitors when they arrive to the town, is so ugly, that it has become "a historical monu
2 CONC ment of the era," and therefore can't be bulldozed to the ground. The English version of Wikipedia posits that:
2 CONT
2 CONT  "However, the term (Sausage Building) is rarely used and is unfamiliar even to most natives of Helsinki." 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''And, at this''' juncture, the English Wikipedia page ''asks a citation'' to support the nonsense for an argument. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Despite the infamy, and the fact that one of the classics of the Finnish cinema [https://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%A4%C3%A4lt%C3%A4_tullaan,_el%C3%A4m%C3%A4 Here We Come, Life!], sort of a Finnish version of the [https://en.wikip
2 CONC edia.org/wiki/Rebel_Without_a_Cause Rebel Without a Cause]  ends with the main character falling from the "sausage" surrounding the building. Surely nobody who ever saw Rebel Without a Cause remembers the observatory either. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In an interesting''' and even a strange contrast to the English page, the Wikipedia in Finnish of the Sausage Building: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  "The building has become an essential part of the collective memory of the people in Helsinki."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''And, indeed it''' has. The largest Finnish newspaper in Finland, Helsingin Sanomat, once published a series called "Helsinki Then and Now." During the 1960's and 1970's Finland suffered from what become know as the "Turku Disea
2 CONC se", given that, during that time, a  huge number of old, beautiful and historically significant buildings were demolished, particularly in the town of Turku, where the term ''functionalism'' served as an euphemism for those who r
2 CONC ooted for East-Berlin-like architorture, and those who were just plain corrupt, and allowed the things to just happen that way. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''"If there's a''' beautiful house, jugend, neoclassicism, what-have-you, let's tear it all down and replace the spots with cubicles." In Helsinki, much less damage was allowed to happen, but it could be argued that Revell single
2 CONC -handedly caused more damage to the facades of Helsinki than the Russian bombing raids during the  WW II ever did. In Turku, Revell's [https://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/KOP-kolmio KOP Corner] always ranks at the top of the ugliest bui
2 CONC ldings in the town, even after the demolition plague is long gone. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During the WW II''' Revell served in the Navy, on the Battleship Ilmarinen. Battleships in the Finnish Navy were totally superfluous given that they only operated on the Baltic Sea, and it was not as if Finland is about to go t
2 CONC o war with some remote places, such as Australia. The battleship [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_coastal_defence_ship_Ilmarinen Ilmarinen] sunk in 1941 when hitting a friendly (own) mine, and Revell was one of the 132 who s
2 CONC urvived, thus joining ''The Ilmarinen Swimming Society'', and where 271 men drowned, alas no Revell. In 1943 Revell was well enough to accept an invite of Neufert to witness the German building standardization efforts, including t
2 CONC he construction of government buildings designed by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_Speer Albert Speer] for the Nazi government. Boy, did he learn!
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.mfa.fi/arkkitehtiesittely?apid=3869
2 CONT
