1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marianne's research from eg.: from national archives, other archives and old books. Everything is written here by Marianne N. from Copenhagen, Denmark:
2 CONT
2 CONT All the children from Philip Gosche Michael Schultz and Catharine Margrethe Trane; 18 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 deadborn children,
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 living children where 5 daughters and 2 sons was alive in may 1801:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 sons in 1801:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1758 - 1823) Carl Heinrich August Schultz
2 CONT
2 CONT (1762 - 1822) Philip Jacob William Schultz
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 daughters in 1801:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1750 - 1808) Lucie Christiane Schultz
2 CONT
2 CONT (1761 - 1805) Phillippina Cecilia Maria Schultz
2 CONT
2 CONT (1764 - 1829) Charlotte Amalia Augusta Schultz
2 CONT
2 CONT (1766 - after 1808) Frederikke Margrethe Schultz
2 CONT
2 CONT (1769 - after 1850) Christiane Hedevig Schultz
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of the other children there is dead before 1801:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1756 - before 1787) Hedwig Eleonora Schultz
2 CONT
2 CONT (bef. mar 21 1759 - 1796) Ulrikke Sofie Schultz
2 CONT
2 CONT (1762 - 1782) Sophia Magdalena Schultz (twin w. Philip J. W. Schultz)
2 CONT
2 CONT Looking for more children born in the years before Lucie born in 1750 and some years after.
2 CONT
2 CONT 55 years married between Philip and Catharine (c. 1746 - 1801)
